+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` currently forwards any input directly to the executor without checking it against the tool's declared `inputSchema`. This spec describes the validation layer that closes that gap: schema validation inside `execute`, compile-time detection of malformed schemas, and redaction of input values from rejection messages so that identifying data never surfaces in log lines or model-visible error text.
+
+## Validation Behaviour
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before invoking the executor. When validation fails it returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the failing constraint; the executor is never called
+  ([validated by: returns a ToolResponse naming the missing required field and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L35)).
+
+- When a field carries the wrong type, the rejection message names the field path and the expected type. It does not echo the offending value, so identifying data present in a tool call cannot leak into the model's context or the server's log stream
+  ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field, naming the path and expected type, without the offending value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L44)).
+
+- A static tool's schema is compiled once at `register` time. If the schema cannot be compiled the call throws synchronously, naming the tool, so a misconfigured tool fails at startup rather than mid-conversation
+  ([validated by: throws at register time for a schema that cannot be compiled, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L54)).
+
+- A rejected tool call returns a `ToolResponse` rather than throwing, so the rejection text becomes a `ToolResultMessage` in the next model round. The model can read the reason and retry with corrected input within the existing `DEFAULT_MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS` budget; `processMessage` resolves instead of propagating an exception
+  ([validated by: resolves processMessage when a tool call is rejected, with the rejection text visible to the provider](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L70)).
+
+## Scope
+
+Validation enforces `required` fields, declared types, and `enum` values. It does not inject `additionalProperties: false`, coerce types, or apply defaults. Unknown keys present in valid input pass through to the executor unchanged. The existing `Unknown tool: <name>` throw for an unregistered tool name is out of scope and stays as-is.
